Subject: Flat Monte Carlo: a counted search that never reads the clock (mtgsim --mc fixed)
Why: Forge's Flat Monte Carlo decides how much to sample by the clock (decision and turn budgets,
  deadlines between rollouts, a cut to the lines the first rollout's time can pay for, a 2 s AI
  timeout inside copies, a pause after slow decisions), so a seeded game with --mc on|max does
  not replay. Adds AiController.setFlatMonteCarloCountOnly: for that player the search size is
  fixed in lines and rounds (Config.counted), the turn budget is 100 rollouts instead of
  seconds, and none of those clock checks run. The counted turn budget is needed: without it a
  play that cannot be put on the stack was chosen again and again until the game timed out
  (3 of 40 games).
Measured: TO BE FILLED

